VALUES ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_coding_k8s_112'), 1, 'Follow one request: which labels does the Service select, which pods carry them, and which port on those pods does the traffic reach? Then check that the Deployment''s selector and its pod labels agree.'),
       ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_coding_k8s_112'), 2, 'Look at `spec.selector.matchLabels` and `spec.template.metadata.labels` of the Deployment, `ports[].name` and `containerPort` of the container, and `selector` plus `port` / `targetPort` of the Service.'),
       ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_coding_k8s_112'), 3, 'A worker that listens on 9000 behind a Service `matcher` on port 80 looks like: Deployment `selector: { matchLabels: { app.kubernetes.io/name: courier-matcher } }`, the same label in the template, `ports: [{ name: grpc, containerPort: 9000 }]`, and a Service with `selector: { app.kubernetes.io/name: courier-matcher }` and `ports: [{ port: 80, targetPort: grpc }]`.');
